# Run Scripts — Use ONLY the Repo `utilities/` Scripts

The ONLY run/launcher/benchmark scripts that may ever be used are the
version-controlled ones in the repo `utilities/` folder, e.g.:

- `utilities/run_glm52.sh` — canonical GLM-5.2-MXFP4 server launcher
- `utilities/e2e_glm5.sh` — end-to-end throughput/latency sweep

A/B is sequential on ONE server: launch `run_glm52.sh` with the feature flag off
(baseline), run `e2e_glm5.sh`, then relaunch with `SGLANG_DSA_FP8_PROJ_GEMM=1`
(feature) and run `e2e_glm5.sh` again. There is no dual-server launcher.

## Hard rules

1. NEVER create, generate, copy, `sed`, or write any run/launcher/benchmark
   script — not locally and not on any remote box.
2. NEVER use or even look at ad-hoc scripts under `/root` (e.g. `/root/run_*.sh`)
   or anywhere outside the repo `utilities/` folder. They are off-limits. The
   repo `utilities/` scripts are the single source of truth.
3. To vary a run, use ONLY the knobs the `utilities/` scripts expose: their
   command-line args (e.g. `--profile`, `--spec`) and the env vars they read
   (`PORT`, `OUT_DIR`, `CONCURRENCY`, and feature flags like
   `SGLANG_DSA_FUSE_INDEXER_QK=1` prefixed on the launch). Do NOT inline a
   hand-rolled `sglang serve` command as a substitute.
4. If no `utilities/` script covers the case, STOP and ask — do not create one
   and do not reach for a `/root` script.
